#
# LeakSanitizer suppressions (chapter 14 §14.8.1, WI-0.558).
#
# Read through LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/asan.supp; lines such as 'leak:<function-or-file-substring>'.
# LSan kinds only: ASan's own kinds (interceptor_*, odr_violation) are read through ASAN_OPTIONS, and a file
# mixing both makes either runtime abort with "failed to parse suppressions".
#
# Every entry sits in a block directly under a comment that links the upstream issue (https://...), with no
# blank line between the comment and the entry. tools/check_suppressions.py enforces this. Procedure:
# docs/dev/sanitizers.md. Keep entries narrow (one function or one file); never suppress OVT code here,
# fix it instead.

# Mesa lavapipe (the only Vulkan ICD on the hosted ubuntu-22.04 runner): one 128-byte realloc made inside the driver
# while the loader enumerates physical devices, in ovt_tests_placebo_probe. https://github.com/openvideotools/ovt/issues/207
# The ICD is dlclose'd by vkDestroyInstance before LSan runs, so its frames are '<unknown module>' and a library-name
# entry can never match; this is the deepest named frame, a loader function that only runs ICD enumeration. It needs
# the full stack, so render/tests/CMakeLists.txt gives that one test binary fast_unwind_on_malloc=0. Remove when a
# run without it is clean.
leak:setup_loader_term_phys_devs
